Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.85,0:00:04.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,Hi, I'm Edwin, student number 25092450.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:05.33,0:00:08.26,Sub,,0,0,0,,Did you know the Atlantic gets about 2 cm wider every year —
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.00,0:00:10.87,Sub,,0,0,0,,roughly as fast as your fingernails grow.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:11.64,0:00:15.25,Sub,,0,0,0,,That's because at the mid-ocean ridge, the plates on either side are moving apart.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:15.25,0:00:17.20,Sub,,0,0,0,,One side's speed is called the half-spreading rate,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.66,0:00:19.53,Sub,,0,0,0,,and both sides together give the full-spreading rate.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:20.76,0:00:21.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,But plates move so slowly —
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.29,0:00:24.17,Sub,,0,0,0,,so how do we know how fast they go?
Dialogue: 0,0:00:24.50,0:00:25.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,This is the mid-ocean ridge.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.65,0:00:27.75,Sub,,0,0,0,,The two paper strips are the seafloor on either side of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.65,0:00:29.15,Anno,,0,0,0,,{\an6\pos(560,640)\fad(220,220)}Mid-ocean ridge\N{\fs28\b0\c&HF0E8E0&}cardboard
Dialogue: 0,0:00:25.75,0:00:27.85,Anno,,0,0,0,,{\an4\pos(1290,560)\fad(220,220)}Seafloor\N{\fs28\b0\c&HF0E8E0&}paper strips
