Dialogue: 0,0:00:38.97,0:00:42.10,Line,,0,0,0,,{\an7\pos(757,662)\fad(260,220)\p1}m 0 -7 b 4 -7 7 -4 7 0 b 7 4 4 7 0 7 b -4 7 -7 4 -7 0 b -7 -4 -4 -7 0 -7{\p0}
Dialogue: 0,0:00:42.20,0:00:47.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,Now suppose this stripe is 100 km from the ridge and 5 million years old.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.20,0:00:49.95,Sub,,0,0,0,,Then the half-spreading rate is 100 km ÷ 5 million years,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:47.20,0:00:51.55,Eq,,0,0,0,,{\an8\pos(960,64)\fad(250,0)}100 km ÷ 5 Myr = 2 cm/yr
Dialogue: 0,0:00:50.05,0:00:51.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,which is 2 cm per year.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:51.95,0:00:53.70,Sub,,0,0,0,,So the seafloor is like a magnetic tape,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:54.17,0:00:56.98,Sub,,0,0,0,,recording every flip of Earth's magnetic field.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:57.59,0:01:00.83,Sub,,0,0,0,,Read the stripes, and we can measure the seafloor spreading rate.
